  "noMusicReason": "Standing rule (2026-08-24 user directive): reels ship voice + SFX only, no music bed by default. Set plan[\"music\"] = true (or a full music object) to opt this reel back into a bed.",
  "format": "news",
  "script": "Your iPhone will install iOS 27.\n\nThat doesn't mean you get the new Siri. What nobody's headline mentioned is the fine print.\n\nSo iOS 27 landed on September 14th, and Apple split it into two separate gates.\n\nHere's the first gate, and it's easy. That includes every iPhone back to the 11, so the software installs almost everywhere.\n\nThen the second gate is where most phones drop out. That's because Siri AI itself needs an iPhone 15 Pro or newer, so 15 Pro, 15 Pro Max, or any 16 and up.\n\nEven clearing that only buys you the base Siri. The version that actually sounds like it's paying attention, with adjustable pace and expressiveness, needs extra processing only the iPhone 17 Pro or iPhone Air can run.\n\nThat's not the end of it either. Then two regions, the EU and China, don't get it at launch at all, both stuck behind regulatory hurdles Apple hasn't cleared.\n\nMeanwhile, it's English-only for now too. French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese and Spanish arrive next month.\n\nAnd one more gate skips hardware completely. Thirteen and up only, no parental workaround.\n\nSo the fine print is four separate gates, not one. Phone, region, language, age.\n\nThen clear all four, and that's when you get the new Siri.",
